# What goes into the .vsix, written as an allowlist rather than as a list of
# things to leave out. `vsce` keeps a file when it matches no pattern here *or*
# matches a negation, so `**` plus negations is the way to say "only these".
#
# The other way round -- naming src/, node_modules/, esbuild.mjs and the rest --
# is a list that goes stale the first time this folder gains a file, and a
# .vsix that ships the source is exactly what bundling was for.
**

!package.json
!README.md
!LICENSE

# The bundle only. Not `dist/**`, which would sweep in an extension.js.map left
# behind by a watch build -- the map carries sourcesContent, so shipping it
# ships the TypeScript. esbuild only emits one under --watch now; this is the
# second half of that, for the copy already on disk.
!dist/extension.js

# By directory, not by the three names in it: media/ is the sidebar's assets and
# the activity-bar icon, and the next one added has to ship too.
!media/**
